  <paragraph>Many of the cells are not filled out. The ones filled in are values that never get past 5, which is the largest legal symbol in base 6, so they are acceptable symbols. But what do we do with 5 + 3 in base 6? We can’t represent the answer as “8” since “8” is not a symbol available to us. Let’s go back to the list of numbers we have for base 6.</paragraph>
  <table>
    <tbody>
      <row>
        <cell>0</cell>
